// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Be Careful What You Wish For
// @category Wishplots / Irony
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Be_Careful_What_You_Wish_For
// @domain   Narrative
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): you get exactly what you wished for — and the getting is the curse; the
// wish is granted, but its fulfilment is itself the ruin. The wisher desired the thing; the thing,
// delivered, brings the disaster (the monkey's-paw twist). Rides the prophecy module: a wish is a
// future-fact a wisher HOLDS as a desire, promoted to the graph by an utterance, then turned
// !absolute! by Fulfills — only here the party FULFILLED is the wisher, and the fulfilment lands
// as catastrophe rather than relief. Sits beside Prophecy Twist (a foretelling fulfilled the
// unforeseen way) and Self-Fulfilling Prophecy (the flight that arrives): all three are the
// prophecy engine's ironic-fulfilment plane. Distinct from a Deal with the Devil — no bargain is
// struck, no price agreed up front; the wish ALONE backfires, the desire's own grant is the cost.
// FRONTIER: the fated $wish is the wisher's OWN ~Desires target, and Fulfills delivers it as a
// curse upon the very one who wished — the grant and the ruin collapse onto one act.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"            // fate, revelation, consequence, cost
import "trl/modules/prophecy.trl"          // Foretell -> ?Fated? ;  Fulfills -> !Fated!, the granted wish

// Lateral thematic links (optional, machine-followable — for discovery / embeddings).
assoc be_careful_what_you_wish_for -> [
  prophecy                : "the ironic-fulfilment engine of",
  prophecy_twist          : "the foretelling-sibling of, fulfilled the unwanted way",
  self_fulfilling_prophecy : "the avoidance-sibling of, on the prophecy plane",
  desire                  : "the wisher's own, turned against him",
  consequence             : "the grant IS the",
  cost                    : "the wish pays itself, no bargain struck"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The granted wish whose fulfilment is the disaster — desire elevated to its own punishment.
imply BeCarefulWhatYouWishFor -> [Reversal, Irony, fate, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule: a wisher DESIRES some $wish and is bound to it as a latent fate (the wish, uttered,
// hangs over him); when that very $wish is FULFILLED — granted to the one who wished it — the grant
// lands as ruin: the wisher is [+Cursed] and the granting deed IS Be Careful What You Wish For.
// The signature that separates it from a plain prophecy: the FULFILLED party and the WISHER are the
// same character ($c desired it, $c is what its granting destroys), and no bargain preceded it.
rule Be_Careful_What_You_Wish_For {
  when:
    char $c [~Desires(target=$wish)]
    char $c [+Fated(to=$wish)]
    evt  $grant [&Fulfills(agent=$any, prophecy=$wish)]
  then:
    $grant [+BeCarefulWhatYouWishFor]
    $c [+Cursed]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: The Monkey's Paw — Mr. White's £200 (W.W. Jacobs, horror short story, 1902) ===
// Warned the talisman grants three wishes that bite, Mr. White wishes for two hundred pounds. The
// wish is granted — as compensation for his son Herbert, killed the next day in the factory machinery.
// He got exactly the sum he asked; the getting was the coffin it paid for.

// MR. WHITE
char white [+Protagonist] [~Desires(target=two_hundred_pounds)]

// HERBERT WHITE — the son
char herbert [+Protagonist]

// THE MONKEY'S PAW — the cursed talisman
obj the_paw [+MacGuffin] [+Cursed]

scene the_wish {
  beat 1 {
    white > the_paw
    evt the_wishing [&Foretells(agent=the_paw, subject=white, fate=two_hundred_pounds)]
    ?white [+Fated(to=two_hundred_pounds)]?      // the wish hangs latent, granted but unrealized
  }
  beat 2 {
    evt the_compensation [&Fulfills(agent=the_factory, prophecy=two_hundred_pounds)]   // the £200, paid for Herbert's death
    !white [+Fated(to=two_hundred_pounds)]!      // the sum arrives — absolute, and ruinous
    herbert [+Doomed]
    // Be_Careful_What_You_Wish_For -> the_compensation [+BeCarefulWhatYouWishFor]; white [+Cursed]
  }
}
